Remarks:
AAP.CE 18 (Articles 7 and 8 of the TM80)

Partial Scope Economic Complementarity Agreement No. 18 (AAP.CE 18) has as its objective to set in place the necessary conditions for the establishment of the common market to be set up pursuant to the Treaty of Asunción dated 26 March 1991, whose main instruments during the transition period are:

• A trade liberalization programme consisting of progressive, linear and automatic tariff reductions, accompanied by the elimination of non-tariff restrictions or measures with equivalent effects; and also of other restrictions on trade between the States Parties, with the aim of achieving zero tariffs by 31 December 1994, without any non-tariff restrictions anywhere in the entire tariff regime;
• The coordination of macroeconomic policies that will be carried out gradually and in convergence with the tariff reduction programmes and programmes to eliminate non-tariff restrictions indicated in the previous section;
• A common external tariff, designed to boost the foreign competitiveness of the signatory countries;
• The adoption of sectoral agreements, designed to optimize the use and mobility of production factors and to achieve efficient operational scales.

In addition, AAP.CE 18 includes provisions on the Origin Regime (Annex I) and safeguard clauses (Annex II).
